-- #1110 origin-agreement corpus — the RESIDUAL section's OCCURRENCE-layer POSITIVE CONTROL.
--
-- The `graph` fixture beside this one produces an occurrence residual with ZERO
-- `graph` rows: every head the graph driver saw acquired an identity. That is a
-- good result, but ON ITS OWN IT IS NOT READABLE — an empty arm is exactly what a
-- section that CANNOT emit that arm would also print, and "the check that reported
-- green was structurally unable to report anything else" is the failure this whole
-- gate exists to prevent. A reviewer looking at the other golden cannot tell the
-- two apart.
--
-- So this fixture makes the graph arm's occurrence residual NON-EMPTY on purpose.
-- `Missing` is declared nowhere, in no module and not in the prelude, so it is
-- resolve.mdk's residual case (1): "the name is in no scope at all". `checkType`
-- reports it as `UnknownType`, errors ACCUMULATE rather than exiting, so the tree
-- still reaches the stamper — which correctly leaves the head `OriginUnresolved`,
-- because there is no module to attribute it to. The golden pins
-- `graph main_unresolved Missing`.
--
-- ⚠️ THAT ROW IS THE CONTROL, NOT A BUG. Deleting `Missing` to "fix" the gate
-- disarms the control and silently returns the occurrence residual to
-- unfalsifiable. If this row ever disappears, the question is what stopped
-- emitting it.
--
-- ⚠️ It must ALSO stay a graph-arm row specifically. The flat and single arms are
-- silent about far more (see the probe's residual section comment), so a residual
-- row from either of them proves nothing about the graph arm's occurrence walk.
--
-- ⚠️ This control covers the OCCURRENCE walk ONLY. It says NOTHING about the
-- `decl:` layer: `fillDeclOrigin` stamps unconditionally whenever it has a module
-- id, and the loader never mints an empty one, so no source program can produce a
-- `graph <slot> decl:X` residual row — that zero is structural, provable only by
-- mutating the compiler, not earned by this or any fixture.
--
-- One module, no imports: the control needs a head the GRAPH path cannot attribute,
-- and adding a module graph around it would only enlarge the golden.

data Parcel = Parcel Int

parcelSize : Parcel -> Int
parcelSize (Parcel n) = n

-- The control itself. `Missing` is intentionally undeclared.
labelOf : Parcel -> Missing
labelOf _ = panic "control fixture: never evaluated"

main = println (parcelSize (Parcel 3))
